 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the Manhasset union free school district and Manhasset\npublic library to take certain actions to correct an understatement in the\ncertification of the 2020-2021 tax levy of the such library",
    "basePrintNo": "S5558",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5558-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5558\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the Manhasset union free school district and Manhas-\nset public library to take certain actions to correct an understatement\nin the certification of the 2020-2021 tax levy of the such library\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo correct a clerical error in the understatement of the certification\nof the 2020-2021 tax levy as it relates to the Manhasset public library,\nto ensure the full amount previously approved by the libraries eligible\nvoters is made available to the library.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe approved budget of the Manhasset Public Library for FY 2020-2021\nrequired raising $5,403,412 in taxes.  In certifying the amount of the\ntaxes to be levied on behalf of the Library during such year, the\nManhasset Union Free School District mistakenly omitted the sum of\n$1,022,625 due to a clerical error.  Accordingly, if left uncorrected,\nthere will be a shortfall or understatement in the amount of $1,022,625\nin taxes levied and collected for such year on behalf of the Library.\n\nThis act corrects the understatement and authorizes the levy and\ncollection of the full amount of the Library's voter approved and\nlawfully authorized taxes for such fiscal year.\n\nThe act authorizes the collection of the FY 2020-2021 understatement in\nthe following FY 2021-2022. Accordingly, over the two-year period,\ntaxpayers would pay exactly the same amount that they have authorized to\nbe raised by taxes. The collection of a portion of that amount would be\ndelayed to the FY 2021-2022 rather than being collected during the year\nfor which it was authorized. The legislation further authorizes the\nSchool District to advance to the Library the amount of the understate-\nment that should have been raised during FY 2020-2021 and be reimbursed\nwhen later is collected in FY 20212022.  Finally, the legislation\nprovides that the Library's tax levy limit should be calculated as if\nthe understatement had not occurred.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would merely authorize the collection of a portion of\nthe taxes authorized to be levied on behalf of the Manhasset Public\nLibrary during FY 2020-2021 to be raised during the following fiscal\nyear, FY 2021-2022. Over the two fiscal years, taxpayers would pay\nexactly the same amount they would have paid if the error did not occur.\nThe will and intent of the voters is being effectuated, upheld and main-\ntained through adoption of this legislation. The taxpayers have previ-\nously authorized this levy and collection of taxes in the amount of\n$5,403,412 during FY 2020-2021 and expect services provided by Manhasset\nPublic Library commensurate with the authorized levy.\n\nIn the absence of this act, the Manhasset Public Library, through no\nfault of its own, would be significantly harmed. The Library would be\ndeprived of the sum of $1,022,625 authorized to be raised on its behalf\nby taxes - or close to 20% of its tax support for the year.\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
